sections.evidence:
- Data loading path and logic: [
  /kaggle/fastai-lesson-05-linear-model-and-neural-net/nb.py.py:19-30
  ] shows loading from Kaggle input or local competition download; [
  /kaggle/fastai-lesson-05-linear-model-and-neural-net/nb.py.py:52-54
  ] reads train.csv into a DataFrame.
- Missing value handling: [
  /kaggle/fastai-lesson-05-linear-model-and-neural-net/nb.py.py:73-85
  ] computes modes and fills NaNs. Runtime evidence confirms NaNs reduced from 866 to 0: [/evidence/artifacts/preprocessing_checks.json:1-24].
- Log transform of Fare: [
  /kaggle/fastai-lesson-05-linear-model-and-neural-net/nb.py.py:115-121
  ]; runtime stats for LogFare are reasonable with no extreme anomalies: [/evidence/artifacts/feature_stats.json:1-40].
- Categorical encoding: [
  /kaggle/fastai-lesson-05-linear-model-and-neural-net/nb.py.py:157-164
  ] uses pd.get_dummies. Columns after dummies include expected categories: [/evidence/artifacts/columns_after_dummies.txt:10-18]. Dummy columns contain only True/False (0/1): [/evidence/artifacts/preprocessing_checks.json:41-78].
- Feature selection and scaling: [
  /kaggle/fastai-lesson-05-linear-model-and-neural-net/nb.py.py:192-200
  ] creates indep_cols and tensor; [
  /kaggle/fastai-lesson-05-linear-model-and-neural-net/nb.py.py:239-241
  ] scales features to 0..1. Runtime evidence shows all scaled feature maxima are 1.0 and minima >= 0: [/evidence/artifacts/preprocessing_checks.json:25-40].
- Text cleanliness: Non-ASCII character counts for Name, Ticket, Cabin are zero: [/evidence/artifacts/preprocessing_checks.json:79-98].
- Sample of raw table head demonstrating correct structure and values: [/evidence/artifacts/train_head.csv:1-12].
- Environment snapshot for reproducibility: [/evidence/artifacts/python_version.txt:1-1], [/evidence/artifacts/pip_freeze.txt:1-200].

- PyTorch ANN uses CPU tensors consistently: [
  /evidence/artifacts/keras-vs-pytorch-a-perfect-guide.py:346-353
]
- PyTorch CNN explicitly moves model and loss to GPU when available: [
  /evidence/artifacts/keras-vs-pytorch-a-perfect-guide.py:565-567
]
- PyTorch CNN explicitly moves batch images and labels to GPU during training and validation: [
  /evidence/artifacts/keras-vs-pytorch-a-perfect-guide.py:579-581,600-602,654-656
]
- PyTorch CNN uses consistent dtypes: images cast to float32 and labels to long during forward/loss: [
  /evidence/artifacts/keras-vs-pytorch-a-perfect-guide.py:585-586,603-605,661-664
]
- No mixed-precision or bf16/float16 policies are set; default fp32 is used consistently across both Keras and PyTorch paths (no occurrences of autocast/mixed precision): grep showed no matches for dtype policy controls in the script.

- The training loss is defined without class weights: [
  /evidence/artifacts/notebook_script.py.py:640-648
] shows criterion = nn.CrossEntropyLoss() with no weight or pos_weight.
- The training DataLoader uses shuffle=True and no sampler: [
  /evidence/artifacts/notebook_script.py.py:600-605
]. The test DataLoader similarly has no sampler or weighting: [
  /evidence/artifacts/notebook_script.py.py:780-785
].
- A targeted search for class-imbalance mechanisms returned no matches: [
  /evidence/artifacts/imbalance_search.txt:1-200
] shows “No matches found” for patterns including class_weight, pos_weight, WeightedRandomSampler, sample_weight, compute_class_weight, SMOTE, or imbalance, and only a plain CrossEntropyLoss is present at line 645.

- CUDA/device usage is commented out and the model remains on CPU: [
  /kaggle/notebook-titanic-nn-randomforest/notebook-titanic-nn-randomforest.py:642-645
].
- Training dataset __getitem__ casts data and labels to float32 consistently: [
  /kaggle/notebook-titanic-nn-randomforest/notebook-titanic-nn-randomforest.py:447-453
].
- Test dataset __getitem__ also casts data to float32: [
  /kaggle/notebook-titanic-nn-randomforest/notebook-titanic-nn-randomforest.py:541-547
].
- Grep summary shows only commented CUDA lines and explicit float32 casts; no active .cuda(), .to(device), autocast, amp, bfloat16, or half usage: [
  /evidence/artifacts/device_dtype_grep.txt:1-200
].

- Preprocessing is fit on training data and applied to test data only: [
  /evidence/artifacts/notebook_code.txt:119-124
] shows:
  - X_processed = preprocessor.fit_transform(X)
  - X_test_processed = preprocessor.transform(X_test)
- Train/validation split from training data only and creation of datasets/loaders: [
  /evidence/artifacts/notebook_code.txt:235-247
].
- Validation used for early stopping and model selection (no test involvement): [
  /evidence/artifacts/notebook_code.txt:200-233
] computes val_loss/accuracy and saves the best model based on val loss.
- Test set only used for inference and submission creation (no labels or fitting): [
  /evidence/artifacts/notebook_code.txt:280-296
] performs inference on test_loader and constructs submission with test_df['PassengerId'].
- Traditional model comparison uses cross-validation on training data (X, y) only: [
  /evidence/artifacts/notebook_code.txt:300-329
] where scores = cross_val_score(pipeline, X, y, cv=5, scoring='accuracy').
- Repository reproducibility hash of the notebook: [
  /evidence/artifacts/notebook_sha256.txt:1-1
] contains the SHA256 of the notebook file.

- The optimizer is constructed with all model parameters: [
  /evidence/artifacts/titanic-tutorial.py:288-293
] shows model creation and optimizer = optim.SGD(model.parameters(), lr=lr) with no parameter freezing.
- The model definition contains no requires_grad modifications or freezing logic: [
  /evidence/artifacts/titanic-tutorial.py:184-200
].
- Runtime instrumentation output confirms all parameters are trainable and updated: [
  /evidence/artifacts/run_log.txt:46-49
] includes "PARAMS total=272, trainable=272" and "TOTAL_PARAM_CHANGE_AFTER_STEP: 0.498190", demonstrating that all parameters require_grad=True and that they change after the first optimizer step.
- Environment snapshot: Python version saved at [/evidence/artifacts/python_version.txt] and partial pip freeze at [/evidence/artifacts/pip_freeze_head.txt].
